wolfSSH v1.4.17: make the Zephyr SFTP server usable for editing files, by
sshfs or any other client.  Applied by freertos/wolfssl/build-wolfssh.sh.

Protocol:
- STAT and LSTAT reply NO_SUCH_FILE for a missing file (sshfs creates a file
  only after hearing that).
- OPEN honours TRUNC (a shorter upload left the old tail) and EXCL.
- SETSTAT and FSETSTAT work: size truncates; owner, mode and times are
  accepted and ignored.  FSTAT works.
- A stat by name syncs open files first: the directory entry lags behind
  writes, and sshfs caches what it hears.

File table (see the comment in src/port.c):
- A real mutex: wc_LockMutex does nothing in a SINGLE_THREADED build, so two
  sessions could share a descriptor.
- A file has one writer.  Conflicting operations close and reopen open files,
  as FatFs has no locking and a second FIL cross-links clusters.
- Rename no longer deletes the file on a case-only rename, deletes the target
  when the source is missing, or orphans a directory moved into itself.

Fixes to existing bugs:
- SFTP_RemoveHandleNode left a dangling list head on removing the newest node.
- READ, WRITE and FSETSTAT copied up to 256 handle bytes into a 4-byte WFD.
- A short write (full card) was reported as success.
- SETSTAT with a bad path replied OK.

